The latest MSTest version is **4.2.3**. Here are the breaking changes relevant to your project:

---

## 1. `[ExpectedException]` is removed (critical for your code)

Your tests use `[ExpectedException]` which is deleted in v4. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

## 2. `Assert.IsTrue(true)` triggers warning MSTEST0032

Your `Validate_ValidInput_Succeeds` test will emit a warning (elevated to Warning severity in v4) for the always-true assertion.

## 3. Other notable v4 breaking changes (not currently affecting your code)

| Change | Impact |
|--------|--------|
| `Assert.ThrowsException` removed | Use `Assert.ThrowsExactly` instead |
| `Assert` message+params signature changed | Use string interpolation for messages |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | `[ClassCleanup]` now always runs end-of-class |
| `TestContext.Properties` is now `IDictionary<string,object>` | Use `.ContainsKey()` not `.Contains()` |
| Dropped .NET < 8 support | Your net8.0 target is fine |
| `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` → `ExecuteAsync` | Only if you have custom test method attributes |

---

